edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399433 1071 "The row echelon form matrix $P$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 7 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399433 1072 #uuid "02830b84-264a-5296-8703-bbcf95ce7d55" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399433 1074 "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $P$ has $3$ pivots in the $2$nd, $3$rd, and $4$th columns:\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 7 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot column is the $1$st column." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399434 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399435 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399434 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399436 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399434 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399437 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399434 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399438 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399434 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399439 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399434 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399434 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399434 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399438 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399434 1080 #uuid "0d5343c6-514b-5142-b39c-cac725e3880e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399435 1081 "$3$rd only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399435 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399435 1084 #uuid "e027a524-8226-530f-8bc1-156c5fd62fd4" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399436 1081 "$1$st and $4$th only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399436 1083 #edb/ref 175921