3478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399467 1084 #uuid "75a25c3a-a40e-586e-8e37-d0e3a0077526" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399468 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399469 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399468 1069 "q-131188" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399468 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399468 1071 "Find the critical points of the function $f(x)=2{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-72x.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399468 1072 #uuid "19a51c3a-961d-51e8-839d-dcbc2e643a8d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399468 1074 "A critical point of $f(x)$ is a point $x=c$ in the domain of $f$ such that either ${f}^{′}(c)=0$ or ${f}^{′}(c)$ does not exist.\n\nDifferentiating $f(x),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-72x) \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}-6x-72.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now proceed to find the critical points:\n\n- First, we compute the points where ${f}^{′}(c)=0.$ We set the derivative equal to zero, and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{2}-6x-72 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-x-12 & =0 \\\\ (x-4)(x+3) & =0 \\\\ x & =-3,\\,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ has stationary points at $x=-3$ and $x=4.$\n\n- Second, we note that ${f}^{′}(x)$ exists for all values of $x$ in the domain of $f(x).$ So $f(x)$ has no non-stationary critical points.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the critical points of $f(x)$ are $x=-3$ and $x=4.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399469 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399470 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399469 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399471 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399469 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399472 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399469 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399473 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399469 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399474 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399469 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399469 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399469 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399471 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399469 1080 #uuid "40b63710-ca14-5f20-99f5-64eef01983af" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399470 1081 "$x=-6$ and $x=3$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399470 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399470 1084 #uuid "efb825ec-4af1-502e-84e4-c2363e24558e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399471 1081 "$x=-3$ and $x=4$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399471 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399471 1084 #uuid "a0005f3d-2f6a-5da0-ad19-56ff2d7b1c97" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399472 1081 "$x=-3$ and $x=6$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399472 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399472 1084 #uuid "40bc473f-1c61-5b45-af07-0768b0375c55" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399473 1081 "$x=-4$ and $x=3$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399473 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399473 1084 #uuid "2ada282e-9a0b-53a0-acf3-911a8863351b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399474 1081 "$x=-4$ and $x=6$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399474 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399474 1084 #uuid "5eb7851c-f9c7-53a1-b68c-803e4833549a" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399475 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399476 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399475 1069 "q-131273" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399475 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399475 1071 "Find the critical points of the function  $f(x)=({x}^{2}-\\frac{5}{4}){e}^{4{x}^{2}}.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399475 1072 #uuid "42598c74-a5de-588f-a397-c6d324d9491a" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399475 1074 "A critical point of $f(x)$ is a point $x=c$ in the domain of $f$ such that either ${f}^{′}(c)=0$ or ${f}^{′}(c)$ does not exist.\n\nDifferentiating $f(x),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(({x}^{2}-\\frac{5}{4}){e}^{4{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & ={({x}^{2}-\\frac{5}{4})}^{′}{e}^{4{x}^{2}}+({x}^{2}-\\frac{5}{4}){({e}^{4{x}^{2}})}^{′} \\\\  & =2x{e}^{4{x}^{2}}+(8x)({x}^{2}-\\frac{5}{4}){e}^{4{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =[2x+8{x}^{3}-10x]{e}^{4{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =(8{x}^{3}-8x){e}^{4{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now proceed to find the critical points:\n\n- First, we compute the points where ${f}^{′}(c)=0.$ We set the derivative equal to zero, and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(8{x}^{3}-8x){e}^{4{x}^{2}} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${e}^{4{x}^{2}}\\ne 0$ for all $x,$ we can divide this equation by ${e}^{4{x}^{2}}$ and solve the resulting equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8{x}^{3}-8x & =0 \\\\ 8x({x}^{2}-1) & =0 \\\\ 8x(x+1)(x-1) & =0 \\\\ x & =0,\\,-1,\\,1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ has stationary points at $x=-1,$ $x=0$ and $x=1.$\n\n- Second, we note that ${f}^{′}(x)$ exists for all values of $x$ in the domain of $f(x).$ So $f(x)$ has no non-stationary critical points.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the critical points of $f(x)$ are $x=-1,$ $x=0$ and $x=1.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399476 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399477 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399476 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399478 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399476 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399479 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399476 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399480 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399476 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399481 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399476 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399476 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399476 1079 #edb/ref 175