ce any numbers $x$ and $y$ are solutions to the third equation $0x+0y=0$, we can remove this equation from the system. So, the corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y=-1 \\\\ y=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation we have $y=4$ and substituting this into the first equation yields $x=-9.$ So,  we conclude that the system is consistent independent. \n\nAs a result, only statement I is true." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399532 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399533 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399532 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399534 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399532 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399535 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399532 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399536 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399532 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399537 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399532 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399532 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399532 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399534 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399532 1080 #uuid "62ec4d2b-adce-53b9-bdc4-0b08d9bbcf9a" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399533 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399533 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399533 1084 #uuid "baed0cbf-38ec-5d81-9809-43dafa9379a2" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399534 1081 "I only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399534 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399534 1084 #uuid "586150d0-53a3-501e-a821-68c180a394cd" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399535 1081 "III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399535 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399535 1084 #uuid "a39c1a3e-21c9-5508-8921-b8a05957b672" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399536 1081 "None" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399536 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399536 1084 #uuid "2247b748-8cef-53eb-82f9-2487685f5057" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399537 1081 "II only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399537 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399537 1084 #uuid "77d955a7-8c55-5d69-9764-f442198cee4b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399538 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399539 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399538 1069 "q-131722" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399538 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399538 1071 "Consider the following system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 3x-3y=6 \\\\  & -2x+y=-3 \\\\  & 4x-4y=8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The system is consistent dependent\nII. The system is consistent independent\nIII. The system has no solution" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399538 1072 #uuid "4890e1ff-ed9a-5558-acd1-bcef01439e04" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399538 1074 "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ are solutions to the third equation $0x+0y=0$, we can remove this equation from the system. So, the corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y=2 \\\\ y=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation we have $y=-1$ and substituting this into the first equation yields $x=1.$ So,  we conclude that the system is consistent independent. \n\nAs a result, only statement II is true." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399539 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399540 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399539 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399541 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399539 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399542 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399539 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399543 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399539 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399544 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399539 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399539 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399539 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399544 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399539 1080 #uuid "cb13c3f2-95da-5f1e-8dd8-8f023abfea3e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399540 1081 "I only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399540 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399540 1084 #uuid "1c927d7e-5c4b-5882-8721-adc2b5fd92e3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399541 1081 "III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399541 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399541 1084 #uuid "64d69900-4157-5d22-aa0e-f4d914c8f721" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399542 1081 "None" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399542 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399542 1084 #uuid "2aba7c87-fdf8-526c-bf60-804628ebce56" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399543 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399543 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399543 1084 #uuid "fea224bb-b24d-5ae7-9e7c-a1698eef7494" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399544 1081 "II only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399544 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399544 1084 #uuid "a62e5405-e20d-5e9c-833b-ebb37c50b5ed" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399545 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399546 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399545 1069 "q-132204" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399545 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399545 1071 "Find the center and radius of the osculating circle to the curve $r(t)$ at the point $P(0,0)$ where $t=0,$ given that $‖{r}^{′}(0)‖=1,$ and the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ to the curve is\n\n$$\nT(t)=⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩.\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399545 1072 #uuid "3e19d212-99bc-5ec6-ba7f-76b0f4f4e8f9" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399545 1074 "Since we are given both the value of $‖{r}^{′}(0)‖$ and the unit tangent $T(t)$, we will use the following formula for the radius of curvature:\n\n$$\nR(t)=\\frac{1}{κ(t)}=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNotice that $r(0)=⟨0,0⟩,$ since the point $P(0,0)$ is at the tip of $r(0).$ \n\nNow, we find ${T}^{′}(t)$, ${T}^{′}(0)$ and $‖{T}^{′}(0)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\ {T}^{′}(0) & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡0,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,0⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(0)‖ & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the radius of curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(0) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(0)‖}{‖{T}^{′}(0)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal normal vector at $t=0$ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(0) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(0)}{‖{T}^{′}(0)‖}=⟨1,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the center of the osculating circle is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(0)+R(0)N(0) & =⟨0,0⟩+1\\cdot ⟨1,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,0⟩+⟨1,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399546 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399547 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399546 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399548 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399546 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399549 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399546 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399550 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399546 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399551 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399546 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399546 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399546 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399547 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399546 1080 #uuid "c7e8d157-633b-58f4-9968-e3a163c79d0d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399547 1081 "The center is $⟨1,0⟩$ and the radius is $1$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399547 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399547 1084 #uuid "dc2c4fc2-a754-53f6-ab25-c364e85fb49f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399548 1081 "The center is $⟨1,1⟩$ and the radius is $1$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399548 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399548 1084 #uuid "6c3b49b7-2177-58c7-9dfd-a4e06235e607" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399549 1081 "The center is $⟨1,0⟩$ and the radius is $2$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399549 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399549 1084 #uuid "046dbcd6-e3df-5486-9381-db7ac7f22442" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399550 1081 "The center is $⟨0,-1⟩$ and the radius is $1$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399550 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399550 1084 #uuid "946cdf15-ce31-5c87-88df-3ce8a6a5154d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399551 1081 "The center is $⟨1,-1⟩$ and the radius is $2$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399551 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399551 1084 #uuid "1ebc0bb1-5876-5366-9608-8b5ebf54b913" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399552 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399553 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399552 1069 "q-132666" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399552 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399552 1071 "Find the values of $x$ for which the function $f(x)={e}^{2{x}^{2}-6x+3}$ is strictly decreasing." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399552 1072 #uuid "e994daf9-6dc5-55a7-aade-020d8278b5a2" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399552 1074 "The function is strictly decreasing where ${f}^{′}(x)<0.$ Differentiating $f(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x)={e}^{2{x}^{2}-6x+3}(4x-6),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso we need to solve the inequality\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2{x}^{2}-6x+3}(4x-6)<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe exponential function is always positive, so this reduces to\n\n$$\n4x-6<0.\n$$\n\nSolving this inequality, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-6 & <0 \\\\ 4x & <6 \\\\ x & <\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the function is strictly decreasing on the interval $(-\\infty ,\\frac{3}{2}).$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399553 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399554 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399553 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399555 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399553 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399556 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399553 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399557 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [1759218639